The rule in recover_json_object says: "The object scored is the last one inside a code fence when any fence holds one, else the last top-level object in the text" and "A candidate that parses as strict JSON, or as JSON with repeated keys resolved last-wins, is scoreable; one that does not ... is passed over". For the original text, the fence holds A which is not a JSON object, and B after the fence is not a JSON object, so no candidate parses; k_recovery returns NO_OBJECT. For the rewritten text, the added C is a JSON object and is the last top-level object, so k_recovery returns that object. Therefore the answer moves from NO_OBJECT to the object.